WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.170
METE ATAMEL: Let's
see how to run Windows

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.270
Container on Compute Engine.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.670
First, we need a Windows VM.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.850
In Google Cloud Console, go
to the Compute Engine Section

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.740
and create an instance.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.480
Make sure Windows
Server for Containers

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.540
is selected for the boot disk.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:22.620
Create a Windows password
and use that password to RDP

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.170
into the instance.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:31.210
Now let's pull another server
image that includes PowerShell

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.950
and run it as a container.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.990
This will take us
inside the container.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:42.310
Now create a Hello
World PowerShell script

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.140
and exit the container.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.200
Get the container ID
and create a new image

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.450
from the modified container.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.320
Finally, create and
run a container based

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.140
on the image we just created.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.000
There you go.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.060
You're running a Windows
container on Google Cloud.

